  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nFriday Night Through Sunday... \n\nDry, pleasant conditions are on the forecast for the weekend. Upper-\nlevels will be mainly zonal with a shortwave trough overnight \nSaturday connecting to a surface low north of the Great Lakes. \nThis will sweep a weak boundary through our area Sunday morning\nbringing a shift in the winds from southerly to northerly. Due \nto low moisture content, we are expecting dry frontal passage \nwith some passing high clouds. Mostly clear skies, with \nrelatively light winds, and low moisture means the weekend \nshould be very nice for any outdoor activities. Highs will sit \ncomfortably in the 60s to 70s. With the northerly winds, we \nshould see lows go from 50s Saturday evening, to 40s Sunday \nnight. \n\nNext Week...\n\nHigh pressure will set up over the area for the start of the week, \nwhich will continue the pleasant weather. Another weak shortwave \ntrough could bring a slight chance for rain along a cold front \nWednesday, but probs are very low (<15%) due to lacking moisture \nreturn. A wind shift and some passing clouds will be the main sign \nof a passing system, with dry frontal passage seeming more likely at \nthis time.",
